                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d9266a61-63c1-4e4c-9d8f-1d0c6272ef20",
                        "source_entry_id": "ea1fc5ac-8596-3d8a-86a4-5d78e8111a60",
                        "source_sense_id": "5bc7a398-2aac-3ec2-b2a3-dc935b085ba9",
                        "target_lang_word": "criminological",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "criminological",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "47e1e758-b094-3802-a6b3-6cefdfd50424",
                                        "entry_id": "97c30191-986d-33be-84e8-cff896e6f658",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or pertaining to criminology."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba5aa7f4-3102-496f-b605-6260111eb196",
                                                "sense_id": "47e1e758-b094-3802-a6b3-6cefdfd50424",
                                                "text": "In my own opinion, “criminal religious movements” (CRMs) is a more accurate and useful category than “cults.” It uses, although selectively, elements from the criminological tradition. It avoids the word “cult” and tries to disentangle the category from both the folk psychology of brainwashing and the politics of “extremism” in theology."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "96506d54-0313-4949-8211-469af61b0cc5",
                        "source_entry_id": "ea1fc5ac-8596-3d8a-86a4-5d78e8111a60",
                        "source_sense_id": "5bc7a398-2aac-3ec2-b2a3-dc935b085ba9",
                        "target_lang_word": "criminologique",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "criminologique",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "26a12861-499b-343d-b0e6-68c70e182abe",
                                        "entry_id": "a99a5354-e6ef-3ff3-830c-b1d50ddf2a60",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Relatif à la criminologie."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "16b4bd55-81f4-4493-8aee-cce51cc94d38",
                                                "sense_id": "26a12861-499b-343d-b0e6-68c70e182abe",
                                                "text": "L’équipe de la bourse coordonnée de recherches criminologiques chargée d’étudier la criminalité des femmes a définitivement mis au point son étude qui sera soumise au CDPC en vue de son adoption et de sa transmission au Comité des Ministres."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d37f065-fc20-4178-a94f-ecbda96a0f75",
                                                "sense_id": "26a12861-499b-343d-b0e6-68c70e182abe",
                                                "text": "Un troisième modèle, plus récent, préconise une séparation entre les interventions pénales et les interventions sociales afin d’éviter la confusion, souvent dénoncée dans la littérature criminologique, entre les valeurs punitives et les valeurs éducatives, entre l’aide et la répression."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b2091b4d-0993-41d3-979c-4a04c898ecdf",
                                                "sense_id": "26a12861-499b-343d-b0e6-68c70e182abe",
                                                "text": "« Quand on nous pose la question de la dangerosité, on distingue la dangerosité psychiatrique et la dangerosité criminologique », complète-t-il."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "20dfcfc7-ac58-4c04-b67b-4f7a932082d0",
                        "source_entry_id": "ea1fc5ac-8596-3d8a-86a4-5d78e8111a60",
                        "source_sense_id": "5bc7a398-2aac-3ec2-b2a3-dc935b085ba9",
